00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.280
A concentrated rally occurs when a handful

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.260
of large cap names drive most of the index gains,

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.380
leaving smaller stocks and other sectors behind.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.800
Europe's equity market has flipped

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.820
from its traditional broad participation

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.960
into exactly this pattern in 2026.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.440
Mirroring the US experience where a few mega-cap AI stocks

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.300
have dominated.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.760
The Bloomberg Market's report notes

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.780
that the European equity market had long been viewed

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:30.400
as immune to shocks driven by only a handful of stocks,

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.000
yet a narrow rally this year has completely flipped that script.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.600
For Canadian investors, this matters

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.800
because the same dynamic can appear on the TSX

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.820
when resource or financial names lag behind a few dominant names.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.060
One practical way to monitor it is to compare

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.220
the equal-weighted version of an index

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.640
against the cap-weighted version using free charting tools

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:55.180
on trading view or your broker platform.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.440
A widening gap signals concentration risk.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.620
Historically, this setup has produced sharp reversals

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:05.340
when leadership rotates, but it can also persist for months,

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.260
punishing diversified portfolios that hold the broader index.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.820
The risk is that a sudden policy or earning shock

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.260
in the leaders triggers a broad sell-off.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.840
Check the 20-day volume on the leaders

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.380
versus the broader index before assuming the trend will continue.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.120
This is the exact scenario where our earlier rule

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.440
of a volume confirmation would have helped.

