00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:45.140
Now here is something that most retail investors get wrong

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.740
and it cost me money before I figured it out.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.880
Imagine you added an Ethereum ETF to your TFSA last week

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.500
after seeing five straight days of inflows.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.960
Your purchase executed at the prevailing market price

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:02.060
yet the very next day the fund posted net outflows

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.180
and the price dropped.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.760
What actually happened is that authorized participants

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:10.140
create or redeem ETF shares in large blocks

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:12.600
only when arbitrage opportunities appear

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:14.560
between the ETF's market price

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.700
and the underlying crypto holdings.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.420
Retail flows alone do not force immediate price movement.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.960
In the most recent week Ethereum ETFs recorded

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:25.900
a net outflow on the final day

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.760
even while extending their three week inflow streak

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.200
showing how daily noise can mask the longer trend.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:35.880
Bitcoin ETFs logged a second day of outflows

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.660
yet also kept their weekly inflow streak alive

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:39.640
at three weeks.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.520
The pro tip most retail investors miss

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.700
is to look at the premium or discount

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:47.260
to net asset value reported each morning

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.320
on the issuer site before trading.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.800
A persistent discount can signal that selling pressure

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.160
is already priced in.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.180
The biggest mistake with ETF flow data

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:00.300
is treating one day's print as a directional signal.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.980
Instead, always average the last five trading days

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:07.460
and cross check against the underlying asset spot volume.

